    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A 48-hour miso cure, then five minutes under the broiler. That is the whole recipe, and the long wait is doing something specific: sak&eacute;, miso and coconut sugar reduced to a glaze, then given two days to work into the fillet so the caramelised edge is not just a coating on the outside.</p><p>Built into bento boxes it becomes a week of lunches. The salmon is as good at room temperature as it is warm, which is unusual for fish and the reason this one is built for meal prep rather than for dinner tonight.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
