    "game_plan": {
      "type": "timeline",
      "blocks": {
        "s_thaw": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/miso-bento-01-ingredients.jpg",
            "subheading": "The night before",
            "heading": "Thaw the fillets and gather everything",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Move the sealed packs from the freezer to the refrigerator about 12 hours ahead. You will also want sak&eacute;, miso, coconut sugar, sushi rice, broccolini, avocado, pickled red onions, scallions and a tin of salmon roe.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_glaze": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/miso-bento-02-sake-miso-reduction.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 1",
            "heading": "Reduce the sak&eacute;, miso and sugar",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Half a cup of sak&eacute; to a gentle simmer. Whisk in the miso until it fully dissolves, then the coconut sugar. Keep it moving for about 10 minutes until it thickens and reduces by half. It catches easily at the end, so do not walk away.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_cool": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/miso-bento-03-marinade-cooling.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 2",
            "heading": "Cool it completely &mdash; this one matters",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Into a shallow bowl and straight into the refrigerator for 10&ndash;15 minutes. Warm marinade starts cooking the surface of the fish, and you lose the texture the cure is supposed to give you. Cold to the touch before it meets the salmon.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_fillets": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/miso-bento-04-king-salmon-fillets.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 3",
            "heading": "Dry the fillets and check for pin bones",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Rinse under cold water and pat thoroughly dry. Run your fingers along the flesh and pull any pin bones with tweezers. Dry fish takes the cure evenly; wet fish dilutes it.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_marinate": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/miso-bento-05-salmon-in-marinade.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 4",
            "heading": "Two days in the refrigerator",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Fillets into a shallow dish, marinade poured over, every surface coated. Cover and refrigerate 48 hours, turning once at the halfway point. Reserve a little marinade for brushing before it goes under the heat.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
