    "broiler_note": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "name": "t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "section_id": "the-broiler",
        "liquid": "\n<style>\n  .sea-two { --ink:#171717; --muted:#5c5c5c; --line:#e5e2dc; --wash:#faf8f4; --accent:#D45A3C; color:var(--ink); }\n  .sea-two__eyebrow { font-size:11px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--accent); font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px; }\n  .sea-two__heading { font-size:clamp(22px,3.2vw,31px); line-height:1.22; margin:0 0 14px; font-weight:600; }\n  .sea-two__lede { font-size:17px; line-height:1.65; color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 26px; max-width:62ch; }\n  .sea-two__grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:16px; }\n  .sea-two__card { border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; background:var(--wash); padding:20px 22px; }\n  .sea-two__card--fix { border-color:var(--accent); }\n  .sea-two__tag { display:inline-block; font-size:10px; letter-spacing:.08em; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; padding:3px 9px; border-radius:999px; margin:0 0 9px; background:var(--ink); color:#fff; }\n  .sea-two__card--fix .sea-two__tag { background:var(--accent); }\n  .sea-two__name { font-size:17px; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 7px; line-height:1.3; }\n  .sea-two__note { font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.6; color:var(--muted); margin:0; }\n  .sea-two__foot { font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.6; color:var(--muted); margin:20px 0 0; padding-top:14px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); max-width:70ch; }\n  @media (max-width:749px) { .sea-two__grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"sea-two\">\n  <p class=\"sea-two__eyebrow\">The only part that can go wrong</p>\n  <h2 class=\"sea-two__heading\">Five minutes at the broiler, and you do not leave it.</h2>\n  <p class=\"sea-two__lede\">\n    There is sugar in this glaze, and sugar under a broiler goes from caramelised to black in\n    well under a minute. Everything else in this recipe is forgiving. This is the part that is not,\n    and it is the reason to scrape the excess marinade off before the fish goes in rather than\n    leaving a thick layer that will burn before the centre is warm.\n  </p>\n\n  <div class=\"sea-two__grid\">\n    <div class=\"sea-two__card\">\n      <span class=\"sea-two__tag\">What goes wrong</span>\n      <p class=\"sea-two__name\">Thick marinade, unattended pan</p>\n      <p class=\"sea-two__note\">\n        Excess marinade scorches and turns bitter while the fillet is still cold in the middle.\n        Broilers are also wildly uneven, so one end of the tray browns minutes ahead of the other.\n      </p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"sea-two__card sea-two__card--fix\">\n      <span class=\"sea-two__tag\">What to do</span>\n      <p class=\"sea-two__name\">Scrape, brush thin, rotate halfway</p>\n      <p class=\"sea-two__note\">\n        Scrape the excess, brush on one fresh thin layer, and turn the tray at the halfway mark.\n        Pull it around 130&deg;F &mdash; it climbs to roughly 150&deg;F while it rests, which is\n        exactly where you want it.\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <p class=\"sea-two__foot\">\n    If your broiler runs hot, drop the rack one level rather than shortening the time. You want the\n    glaze to caramelise and the fillet to warm through at roughly the same rate.\n  </p>\n</div>",
        "padding_top": 12,
        "padding_bottom": 44,
        "divider": false,
        "narrow": false,
        "rounded": false,
        "color_text": "",
        "color_background": "",
        "gradient_background": "",
        "color_button_text": "",
        "color_button_background": "",
        "color_button_gradient": ""
      }
    },
