        },
        "m_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>That cadence is the whole point of the 48 hours. The fish thaws while you are at work, goes into the marinade that evening, and is ready to broil on Sunday when you are already in the kitchen.</p><p>Sealed boxes keep for three or four days. The salmon holds its caramelised edge cold, so there is nothing to reheat &mdash; which is the difference between meal prep you actually eat and meal prep that sits there.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
